Description: Launch an executable chosen as a handler through GIO, so that it can run in a scope of its own.
 Firefox launches applications from desktop entries through GIO, but runs an executable chosen as the handler of a
 MIME type or URI scheme, or named by a mailcap file, with nsIProcess. Such a handler runs in Firefox's own cgroup,
 so it ends together with Firefox when systemd-oomd kills Firefox's scope or systemd stops it, and GLib cannot start
 it in a systemd scope of its own. It also receives no activation token on Wayland, and inherits MOZ_APP_LAUNCHER,
 which GIO launches unset (Mozilla bug 1494436).
 .
 nsIGIOService::CreateAppFromExecutable() describes the executable as a desktop entry whose Exec key passes the URI
 unchanged (%u with X-GIO-NoFuse) or the path of the local file (%f). nsLocalHandlerApp::LaunchWithURI() launches it
 with a URI and the new nsMIMEInfoBase::LaunchAppWithFile() with a file, through nsGIOMimeApp::LaunchWithURI(),
 which requests the activation token on Wayland. Both fall back to nsIProcess when GLib refuses the executable: when
 it is no executable file, so that nsIProcess reports the error, and when its path contains %, as GLib checks the
 Exec key before it turns %% back into %.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-08
